.TH TULPAR-REINSTALL 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.7.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-reinstall \- reinstall installed packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar reinstall
.RI [ options "] " "package|file.apg" ...
.br
.B tulpar R
.RI [ options "] " "package|file.apg" ...
.br
.B tulpar \-R
.RI [ options "] " "package|file.apg" ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs the same version of an already installed package again, which
restores files that were deleted or modified. For a package name, the
installed version is fetched from the configured repositories. For a
path to a
.B .apg
file, the archive is used directly and must contain the installed
version of an installed package. Whether a package was installed
explicitly or as a dependency is preserved, and held packages are
refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes and skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show the transaction without writing anything to disk.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Reject packages that fail signature verification.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate on the database of an alternate root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if a package is not installed, the matching version
cannot be found, or the transaction fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-verify (1),
.BR tulpar-install (1)
